<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 25 May, from 567 BCE to 1977.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/servius-tullius" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/servius-tullius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">567 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,592 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Servius Tullius celebrates a triumph over the Etruscans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">According to the Fasti Triumphales, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/servius-tullius">Servius Tullius</a>, by Roman tradition the sixth king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, celebrated a triumph over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a>, one of three he held. Early in his reign he had warred against Veii and the Etruscans.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/servius-tullius">Servius Tullius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-triumph">Roman triumph</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1085">1085 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">941 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alfonso VI of Castile takes Toledo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> after its Muslim ruler surrendered. The old Visigothic capital became a centre where Christian, Jewish and Muslim scholars translated Arabic learning into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI of Castile</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1420">1420 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">606 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prince Henry the Navigator becomes administrator of the Order of Christ</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Prince Henry the Navigator</a> was appointed administrator of the Order of Christ, the Portuguese successor to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Knights Templar</a>, based at Tomar. He held the post for life, and the order's revenues helped to fund his voyages.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Prince Henry the Navigator</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-christ-portugal">Order of Christ</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1521">1521 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles V issues the Edict of Worms against Luther</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The emperor declared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> an outlaw and banned his writings. Protected by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-elector-of-saxony">Frederick the Wise</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wartburg">Wartburg</a>, Luther began translating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-testament">New Testament</a> into German.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1787">1787 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">239 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constitutional Convention opens in Philadelphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates reached a quorum at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a> State House and chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> to preside. Over the summer they drafted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-the-united-states">US Constitution</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1803">1803 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">223 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ralph Waldo Emerson is born in Boston</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emerson became the leading voice of Transcendentalism. Essays such as 'Self-Reliance' shaped American thought and influenced Thoreau and Whitman.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1961">1961 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kennedy commits America to landing on the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Addressing Congress, President Kennedy called for a man to be landed on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a> and returned safely before the decade was out. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> 11 met the goal in July 1969.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1977">1977 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">49 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Star Wars opens in American cinemas</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">George Lucas's space adventure opened in a few dozen cinemas and became the highest-grossing film to that date. It reshaped Hollywood around the blockbuster and merchandising.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 25 May <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-suko"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-suko.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Sukō</span><span class="tp">1334–1398</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/minh-mang"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/minh-mang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Minh Mang</span><span class="tp">1791–1841</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/u-nu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/u-nu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">U Nu</span><span class="tp">1907–1995</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/basdeo-panday"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/basdeo-panday.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Basdeo Panday</span><span class="tp">1933–2024</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 25 May <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/aldhelm"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aldhelm.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Aldhelm</span><span class="tp">c. 639–709</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-i"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Mieszko I</span><span class="tp">c. 930–992</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-gregory-vii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Gregory VII</span><span class="tp">c. 1015–1085</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pedro-calderon-de-la-barca"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pedro-calderon-de-la-barca.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pedro Calderón de la Barca</span><span class="tp">1600–1681</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-durban"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/benjamin-durban.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Benjamin D'Urban</span><span class="tp">1777–1849</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/symon-petliura"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/symon-petliura.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Symon Petliura</span><span class="tp">1879–1926</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/idris-of-libya"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/idris-of-libya.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Idris of Libya</span><span class="tp">1890–1983</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
